            <ArticleTitle>Polyarteritis nodosa and the antiphospholipid syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1210-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of classical polyarteritis nodosa (PAN) with visceral aneurysms presenting with renal infarction and hypertension. The female patient also had all the laboratory features of the antiphospholipid syndrome (APS) and 2 months into her illness developed a large iliofemoral thrombosis. She responded well to immunosuppressive therapy and anti-coagulation. Repeat arteriogram showed regression of the visceral aneurysms. The link between PAN and APS, and the therapeutic dilemma posed by this association, are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
